    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey can u give me a quick breakdown of the stages for a standard CI/CD pipeline? specifically i need the stages for code commit, automated testing, staging, and production deployment. also just include what kind of gates/checks should be at each stage so we can make sure nothing breaks. thanks",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A standard CI/CD pipeline typically begins with an automated pull request verification that checks for code formatting, license compliance, and initial unit test passes before merging to the main branch. Once a change is successfully merged, it triggers an automated staging deployment where heavier integration tests and security scans run to ensure the application functions correctly across different environments. Finally, upon passing all stage-specific gates which define strict failure criteria for each step, the system performs a manual or auto-approval production deployment and runs smoke tests to confirm live availability. This gated approach ensures that code only proceeds to the next stage if it meets rigorous quality and stability standards.",
      "source": "target",
